# Requests for the API panel (and VS Code's REST Client or JetBrains' HTTP client).
# Paths are relative to the server, which listens on the port it prints. Start it with
# Run (go run .), then send these.

### Say hello
GET /hello?name=Gopher

> status 200
> json $ == {"message": "hello, Gopher"}

### Read the notes table (load scratch.sql first: psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f scratch.sql)
GET /notes

> status 200
> json $[*].title == ["Read the Go 1.27 release notes", "Try range over a function", "Write a table test"]
